  "prompt": "Is residential rent of ₱15,000 per month VAT-exempt?",
  "runtimeCommit": "bd19b3d7a220132a618a3777a33fdfa0b34099ea",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe residential rent of ₱15,000 per month is VAT-exempt under Philippine tax law.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor landlords renting out residential properties at ₱15,000 or less per month, they do not need to register as VAT taxpayers or charge VAT on the rent. This exemption can be beneficial for both landlords and tenants, as it simplifies the rental transaction and reduces costs for tenants. Landlords should ensure that their rental agreements reflect this exemption to avoid any potential tax liabilities.",
